      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "i do have a similar issue as vivithecanine where i don't have a proper internet connection for this and next year and instead have to rely on an LTE connection for daily internet use with sometimes going as low as 2MBit/s.\n\nIn general i feel like it would be great to provide powerusers with the ability to control yt-dlp as one likes to.\n\nThe idea to just point the config file location in the same directory where yt-dlp resides for VRC would be pretty sufficient already, or perhaps even provide an option in the games/Steam launch parameters to point the config file to a custom directory via `--config-location`, so that we won't run into [this](https://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/video-players-do-not-work-if-a-yt-dlp-user-configuration-is-present) issue again.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
